    <span class="eyebrow">For Parents & Teachers</span>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,4.5vw,2.6rem);color:var(--teal-dark);">A quick, honest overview</h1>
    <p>Koa's Beach Adventures is a 20-book picture book series following a koala and a seagull across the Pacific, meeting a new local animal — and a new real place — in every book. Each story is built around curiosity, kindness, friendship, culture, and caring for nature, with environmental action as one expression of that, never the whole lesson.</p>
    <p>The series is genuinely tied to a real initiative, <a href="/about/#catalyx-one">Catalyx One</a>, currently focused on sorting and recycling household waste across the Pacific, with a future funding-dependent stage aimed at converting waste into energy. We're specific about which stage is real and which is aspirational — see the About page for the honest breakdown.</p>
    <p>Cultural sensitivity is a standing rule across the series: no living cultural or religious art traditions are used as decoration on characters. Character designs use landscape-inspired or invented patterns only.</p>
    <p><strong>Coming to this page:</strong> downloadable classroom activity packs, printable worksheets, and curriculum-aligned resources, as the series grows. For now, the free <a href="/play/">Colouring Corner and Character Passports</a> are ready to use in a classroom or at home.</p>
